From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:42:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWebView+WebContent: Let the UI prepare a tab to be
 discarded

A UI that discards background tabs to save memory, as Chromium's Memory
Saver does, restores them later from a snapshot of their session
history. The current entry's scroll position only reaches that history
when the user leaves the entry, so a restored tab came back scrolled to
the top.

ViewImplementation::prepare_for_discard() has the page save its
persisted state to the active session history entry, as leaving the
entry does, and says whether a text control holds input that
discarding the tab would lose, so that the UI can leave such a tab
alone. The view also says whether a DevTools client is connected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
